# Runner command wrapper (required)

Every **external** command in `scripts/*`, `scripts/dev/*`, and `scripts/lib/*` must go through the shared runner (`scripts/lib/runner`). This records stdout, stderr, exit status, and cmdline under `RUNNER_SESSION_DIR`, which is created under the default session root `~/scratch/repository-helpers/runner-sessions/` (overridable with `RUNNER_SESSION_ROOT`), so checker emails can reconstruct failures. Stale session directories are pruned on begin (`RUNNER_SESSION_MAX_AGE_DAYS`, default 3).

## Wiring

| Context | Load |
| --- | --- |
| Top-level executable (`scripts/*`, `scripts/dev/*`) | `source "${script_dir}/lib/runner-bootstrap"` early |
| Sourced library (`scripts/lib/*`) | `source "${lib_dir}/runner-ensure"` (idempotent re-source guard if the lib may load twice) |

## Which helper to use

| Helper | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| `run_command` | Default — stream stdout to caller, print `[FAIL]` diagnostics on stderr |
| `run_command_or_die` | Fatal step |
| `runner_exec` | Capture only (no stdout replay) |
| `runner_exec_stdout` | `var="$(…)"` substitution |
| `runner_sh` / `runner_sh_stdout` | Pipelines, `(cd dir && …)`, compound shell |

Optional flag on the helpers above: `--timeout SECONDS` (GNU `timeout` / `gtimeout`).
On expiry the helper exits **124** and prints one `ERROR: WAIT_TIMEOUT <label> timeout=<Ns>` line.
Ctrl-C prints `[INT] Interrupted: <label>` plus the quoted cmdline, then kills the child (exit 130).

## Do not wrap

- Bash builtins (`cd`, `echo`, `printf`, `[[`, etc.)
- `command -v` prerequisite probes
- Intentional background streaming where the parent already tees output
- `tests/*` harness mocks

## Do not add pass-through wrappers

Call `runner_sh_stdout` / `runner_exec_stdout` directly unless the helper encodes real logic (e.g. `cd "$dir" && …` directory helpers). Thin rename wrappers add noise without value.

## Exceptions (document in code + ratchet skip)

- `scripts/lib/ci-secret-scan` — copied verbatim to consumer `.github/ci/secret-scan` with no `runner-ensure` beside it (see `tests/lib/runner-adoption-count` skip list).

## Enforcement

- `tests/runner-adoption.test` ratchet: **zero** bare external invocations (`tests/fixtures/runner-adoption-baseline.txt` must stay `0	__TOTAL__`).
- Checker emails use `runner_report_append_command_failures` / child `command_failures` JSON — bare commands leave nothing to report.

```bash
# BAD
git -C "$repo" fetch origin

# GOOD
run_command "git fetch origin" --timeout 120 git -C "$repo" fetch --prune origin

# GOOD (capture)
url="$(runner_exec_stdout "gh repo view" --timeout 30 -- gh repo view "$slug" --json url -q .url)"
```
